1
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:12,100
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,633 --> 00:00:32,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:35,100
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,967 --> 00:00:41,333
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:43,833
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,967 --> 00:00:45,067
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,167 --> 00:00:46,133
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:48,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,133
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,467 --> 00:00:53,633
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:55,333
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,633 --> 00:00:58,067
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,167 --> 00:01:00,333
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,967 --> 00:01:03,133
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,167 --> 00:01:06,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,133 --> 00:01:11,667
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,833 --> 00:01:12,867
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,733 --> 00:01:21,967
<i>Stop what you're doing!
The NLEA will handle this.</i>

21
00:01:22,133 --> 00:01:24,600
<i>The NCIA operation
is what led to the ambushes.</i>

22
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:27,667
<i>Stop arguing! Fine.
Do your own investigation, then!</i>

23
00:01:27,833 --> 00:01:31,000
<i>They won't get you.
I'm here to protect you.</i>

24
00:01:31,167 --> 00:01:32,800
<i> I'd risk my life for you.</i>

25
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:35,600
<i>Neighbors!
We've got outsiders!</i>

26
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:37,667
<i>You picked the wrong place
to come into.</i>

27
00:01:37,833 --> 00:01:39,800
<i>If you didn't see anyone,
we'll leave!</i>

28
00:01:39,967 --> 00:01:42,100
This is all your fault, Ricardo.

29
00:01:42,233 --> 00:01:45,500
<i>You never should've let her
into your world!</i>

30
00:01:45,667 --> 00:01:47,633
<i> - If they don't give us Sam...
</i>- [GUN COCKS]

31
00:01:47,733 --> 00:01:50,467
<i>We'll get her back
by whatever means necessary.</i>

32
00:01:50,567 --> 00:01:53,000
<i> And she's even an NCIA agent!</i>

33
00:01:53,167 --> 00:01:56,333
<i> We might get dragged
</i>into the mess she escaped from!

34
00:01:56,433 --> 00:01:58,500
<i> Gabo won't put us in danger.</i>

35
00:01:58,667 --> 00:02:00,167
<i>There are men circling
our neighborhood.</i>

36
00:02:00,267 --> 00:02:01,333
<i> Are they looking for you?</i>

37
00:02:01,433 --> 00:02:02,700
<i>I have something
important to tell you.</i>

38
00:02:02,867 --> 00:02:04,167
But this has to stay between us.

39
00:02:11,167 --> 00:02:15,333
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

40
00:02:15,467 --> 00:02:18,267
[INDISTINCT CONVERSATION]

41
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:25,200
Listen carefully.

42
00:02:26,267 --> 00:02:28,000
What I'm about to tell you
is important.

43
00:02:32,967 --> 00:02:34,200
Do you remember...

44
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:38,533
...the NCIA agent I faced
in our first mission?

45
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:39,933
That fair-skinned woman?

46
00:02:40,067 --> 00:02:43,433
- Didn't I fight her, too?
- Yeah. That's her.

47
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:47,500
Last night, after we went our
ways, and I was in my room...

48
00:02:48,067 --> 00:02:49,767
Something fell from above.

49
00:02:49,933 --> 00:02:51,467
That woman fell
through our roof.

50
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:53,267
She fell through your roof?

51
00:02:53,767 --> 00:02:55,200
How did that happen, Gabo?

52
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:57,900
Maybe she got lost
and went into your room, huh?

53
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,267
Are we gonna be godfathers now?

54
00:02:59,433 --> 00:03:01,033
[IPE] Hey, stop joking around.

55
00:03:01,133 --> 00:03:03,033
Can't you see this is
a serious conversation?

56
00:03:03,133 --> 00:03:10,100
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

57
00:03:14,433 --> 00:03:15,700
[EXHALES]

58
00:03:18,133 --> 00:03:25,100
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

59
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:29,933
[SAM] Where am I?

60
00:03:40,167 --> 00:03:47,133
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

61
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:54,800
<i> Whose house is this?</i>

62
00:03:57,833 --> 00:03:58,967
<i> I see weapons.</i>

63
00:03:59,333 --> 00:04:01,867
<i>It's safe to say whoever
lives here is dangerous.</i>

64
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:09,667
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

65
00:04:12,167 --> 00:04:13,967
[TEKLA] Hang on.
Who are you talking about?

66
00:04:14,367 --> 00:04:15,767
That fair-skinned woman?

67
00:04:17,067 --> 00:04:18,100
She's here?

68
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:19,467
Miss Mameng, is she inside?

69
00:04:19,567 --> 00:04:21,533
Bring her out, come on!
Where's that woman?

70
00:04:21,667 --> 00:04:23,967
She needs to face me
and pay for what she did!

71
00:04:24,067 --> 00:04:25,167
- [GABO] Tekla!
- She wronged me!

72
00:04:25,333 --> 00:04:28,833
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

73
00:04:29,033 --> 00:04:30,000
[MAGAZINE CLICKS]

74
00:04:34,533 --> 00:04:36,133
[TEKLA] Oh, absolutely not!
Where is she?

75
00:04:36,233 --> 00:04:37,667
I've got a score to setttle
with her!

76
00:04:37,833 --> 00:04:39,167
Bring her out!
Show her to me!

77
00:04:39,333 --> 00:04:40,500
- [WHISPERS] Tekla!
- Ouch!

78
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:41,800
Keep it down!

79
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:43,200
[MUMBLES]

80
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:45,367
[GABO] She was shot.

81
00:04:46,333 --> 00:04:48,067
Her life is clearly in danger.

82
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:51,067
[SAM] I know him.

83
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:54,633
<i>He's the same jerk
who disrespected me.</i>

84
00:04:54,733 --> 00:04:57,167
<i>Does that mean I fell
into their house?</i>

85
00:04:57,900 --> 00:05:01,000
Of all the houses to crash into,

86
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:03,033
<i> why did it have to be his?</i>

87
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:05,200
<i>But there's nothing
I can do now.</i>

88
00:05:05,467 --> 00:05:07,200
<i> My life is in danger.</i>

89
00:05:07,367 --> 00:05:09,167
<i> I need to hide here.</i>

90
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:12,700
[VEHICLES APPROACHING]

91
00:05:12,867 --> 00:05:14,700
[TIRES SCREECHING]

92
00:05:14,867 --> 00:05:17,700
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

93
00:05:17,867 --> 00:05:18,867
[MUSIC ENDS]

94
00:05:19,133 --> 00:05:21,233
[MARIANO]
Have you heard from Lucas?

95
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:23,100
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

96
00:05:23,233 --> 00:05:24,367
No news yet.

97
00:05:26,633 --> 00:05:27,700
[DOOR OPENS]

98
00:05:28,133 --> 00:05:29,600
Sir. Ma'am.

99
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:31,167
Several vehicles arrived
at the gate.

100
00:05:31,267 --> 00:05:32,933
Here's the CCTV footage.

101
00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:39,867
It's Ricardo Jacinto.

102
00:05:39,967 --> 00:05:41,633
That's a bold move.

103
00:05:41,767 --> 00:05:43,067
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

104
00:05:43,233 --> 00:05:45,733
[DEBORAH] He's got the nerve
to come here unannounced.

105
00:05:46,267 --> 00:05:47,867
Let them in.

106
00:05:48,433 --> 00:05:50,267
Don't forget to tell our men
to get ready.

107
00:05:50,433 --> 00:05:51,700
Yes, sir. Ma'am.

108
00:05:52,967 --> 00:05:54,567
[ARTURO] Men, open the gates.

109
00:05:54,967 --> 00:05:55,967
Yes, go ahead.

110
00:06:00,733 --> 00:06:01,733
[DRAWER RATTLING]

111
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:03,933
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

112
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:05,633
A little insurance.

113
00:06:09,500 --> 00:06:16,933
[TIRES SCREECHING]

114
00:06:19,467 --> 00:06:20,967
- [CAR DOOR OPENS]
- [TIRES SCREECH]

115
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:25,500
[CAR DOORS CLOSING, OPENING]

116
00:06:25,633 --> 00:06:27,100
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

117
00:06:27,267 --> 00:06:28,267
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

118
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:30,467
[MARIANO] Ricardo!

119
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:32,933
What a surprise!

120
00:06:33,033 --> 00:06:34,300
You should've told me
you were coming!

121
00:06:34,467 --> 00:06:35,667
Where's my daughter?

122
00:06:36,267 --> 00:06:37,900
Why are you looking
for her here?

123
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,267
Just drop the act!

124
00:06:39,833 --> 00:06:40,900
Samantha was ambushed.

125
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,400
To this day,
she's still missing.

126
00:06:42,533 --> 00:06:44,500
- And I'm your prime suspect?
- I know you!

127
00:06:44,667 --> 00:06:46,700
You're the only one who can
do this to my daughter!

128
00:06:46,833 --> 00:06:49,133
[DEBORAH]
Hold off on your allegations.

129
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:51,000
You don't have any evidence.

130
00:06:51,167 --> 00:06:52,433
I'm not talking to you.

131
00:06:52,533 --> 00:06:53,700
[DEBORAH CHUCKLES]

132
00:06:53,833 --> 00:06:58,267
You seem to be forgetting
you're in our property.

133
00:06:58,367 --> 00:07:00,600
Bring out Samantha,
and this conversation is over.

134
00:07:00,833 --> 00:07:03,333
How many times
do I have to tell you this?

135
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:05,467
Your daughter isn't here!

136
00:07:05,667 --> 00:07:06,633
Bring out Samantha!

137
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:11,267
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

138
00:07:11,367 --> 00:07:13,200
Or you won't like
what comes next.

139
00:07:20,767 --> 00:07:23,300
[LOW CHUCKLE]

140
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:27,467
You know all too well
this is my territory, Ricardo.

141
00:07:27,867 --> 00:07:31,033
Careful, or you won't
leave here alive.

142
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:33,667
[MUSIC INTENSIFYING]

143
00:07:33,767 --> 00:07:34,733
Men!

144
00:07:35,067 --> 00:07:38,833
[HEAVY FOOTSTEPS]

145
00:07:42,033 --> 00:07:48,967
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

146
00:07:52,233 --> 00:07:53,733
Boss, we're outnumbered.

147
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:55,100
There's a lot of them.

148
00:07:55,733 --> 00:07:57,033
[CHUCKLES]

149
00:07:57,900 --> 00:08:00,700
You picked the wrong man
to mess with, Ricardo.

150
00:08:01,133 --> 00:08:05,500
I'm not your old lackey
anymore.

151
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:07,867
You can't scare me
into submission.

152
00:08:08,033 --> 00:08:11,000
See how things have changed
around here?

153
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:15,033
Mariano is more powerful
than you now.

154
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:16,733
If it weren't for me,

155
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:19,567
you wouldn't be
where you are now.

156
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:22,300
You were nobody then.

157
00:08:23,333 --> 00:08:24,900
You're still nobody now.

158
00:08:25,067 --> 00:08:26,533
Everything I have now

159
00:08:26,633 --> 00:08:28,600
is because of my own strategy!

160
00:08:29,467 --> 00:08:33,033
If I were you, I'd leave.

161
00:08:33,467 --> 00:08:34,967
If I lose my temper,

162
00:08:35,767 --> 00:08:38,300
I might bury you alive
right here on my land!

163
00:08:38,433 --> 00:08:42,900
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

164
00:08:43,067 --> 00:08:44,100
Boss!

165
00:08:54,100 --> 00:08:57,933
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

166
00:08:58,633 --> 00:09:00,167
I'm not done with you yet.

167
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:03,633
If anything happens to Samantha,

168
00:09:05,633 --> 00:09:07,567
I'll come back for you.

169
00:09:10,033 --> 00:09:11,967
You'll regret crossing me.

170
00:09:12,500 --> 00:09:13,500
[MARIANO SCOFFS]

171
00:09:13,633 --> 00:09:15,233
Don't worry.

172
00:09:15,333 --> 00:09:17,833
We'll be right here
waiting for you.

173
00:09:18,667 --> 00:09:19,933
But here's a little advice.

174
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:23,433
When you come back,
bring more men next time.

175
00:09:23,967 --> 00:09:25,133
You're short.

176
00:09:26,033 --> 00:09:32,933
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

177
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,533
[RICARDO] I'm not done, Mariano.

178
00:09:42,667 --> 00:09:44,433
<i> We're just getting started.</i>

179
00:09:44,533 --> 00:09:47,300
<i>You may have won today,
but I'll come back for you.</i>

180
00:09:48,133 --> 00:09:49,600
<i>So you want to go after
our children?</i>

181
00:09:49,700 --> 00:09:50,767
<i> Fine.</i>

182
00:09:51,567 --> 00:09:53,133
<i> I'll give you what you want.</i>

183
00:09:53,733 --> 00:09:59,300
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

184
00:09:59,867 --> 00:10:02,133
[TIRES SCREECHING]

185
00:10:02,533 --> 00:10:05,700
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

186
00:10:06,233 --> 00:10:08,367
We need to help and protect her.

187
00:10:09,367 --> 00:10:11,967
Those men who've been lurking

188
00:10:12,067 --> 00:10:14,533
around our neighborhood
are looking for her.

189
00:10:14,667 --> 00:10:16,533
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

190
00:10:16,667 --> 00:10:18,300
[GUNSHOTS]

191
00:10:20,667 --> 00:10:23,067
[SAM] I need to find a way out

192
00:10:24,067 --> 00:10:25,633
<i> before they find me.</i>

193
00:10:30,067 --> 00:10:31,567
We don't know
why they're after her yet.

194
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:34,300
All I know is she's in danger,

195
00:10:34,467 --> 00:10:36,567
and those men
want her dead.

196
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:37,767
[TEKLA] Oh, Gabo.

197
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:39,533
We're going to get dragged
into this again.

198
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:40,833
You know what'd be better?

199
00:10:40,933 --> 00:10:42,833
Why don't we just
tell the police?

200
00:10:42,933 --> 00:10:45,033
She's the one they're
looking for, right?

201
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:46,733
We can't tell the police.

202
00:10:46,867 --> 00:10:48,100
Her life is still in danger.

203
00:10:48,233 --> 00:10:49,667
[BINOY] Those men are armed.

204
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:51,600
They're still hanging around
our neighborhood.

205
00:10:51,733 --> 00:10:53,767
Gabo, son, we could get hurt.

206
00:10:53,900 --> 00:10:55,900
That's why we need
to keep quiet!

207
00:10:56,033 --> 00:10:58,600
Don't tell anyone,
not even our neighbors.

208
00:10:58,733 --> 00:11:00,333
Let's wait until
she gets better,

209
00:11:00,467 --> 00:11:03,367
then we'll ask why
those men are after her.

210
00:11:03,533 --> 00:11:04,667
[TOLITS] On the roof?

211
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:06,500
[SCOFFS]
How'd that happen?

212
00:11:07,033 --> 00:11:08,700
Or did she just wander
into your room?

213
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:10,600
What? Are we going
to be godparents now?

214
00:11:10,733 --> 00:11:11,900
- [LAUGHING]
- Hey!

215
00:11:12,067 --> 00:11:13,033
Get serious.

216
00:11:13,167 --> 00:11:15,100
Can't you see we're having
a serious conversation?

217
00:11:16,567 --> 00:11:18,033
She's with the NCIA.

218
00:11:19,067 --> 00:11:21,400
I'm sure if people
are after her,

219
00:11:22,267 --> 00:11:23,900
they're bad people.

220
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:27,933
[DANTE] Let's just do
everything Gabo says.

221
00:11:35,567 --> 00:11:42,433
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

222
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:47,833
So...

223
00:11:47,933 --> 00:11:50,933
Since Samantha still had not
returned home,

224
00:11:51,033 --> 00:11:54,000
we don't know
if she's still alive or dead.

225
00:11:54,133 --> 00:11:57,000
It seems Ricardo's daughter
is tough.

226
00:11:57,167 --> 00:12:01,100
She's just like her evil father.

227
00:12:02,167 --> 00:12:05,000
Well, whether she's dead
or alive,

228
00:12:05,167 --> 00:12:06,400
the question is...

229
00:12:06,533 --> 00:12:10,233
Does Samantha know
that Lucas shot her?

230
00:12:11,533 --> 00:12:15,000
Tony, how's the search going
on Soriano Street?

231
00:12:15,167 --> 00:12:17,333
Sir, the NLEA has coordinated
with the communities.

232
00:12:17,467 --> 00:12:20,433
The problem is the communities
only refer witnesses to NLEA.

233
00:12:20,567 --> 00:12:23,033
And NLEA's been disrespecting us
since last night.

234
00:12:23,167 --> 00:12:24,700
They're trying
to snatch the case from us.

235
00:12:24,867 --> 00:12:26,433
We have to find a way around it.

236
00:12:26,567 --> 00:12:28,167
The person we're looking for
is from the NCIA.

237
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:30,700
We should be the ones
handling the investigation.

238
00:12:30,867 --> 00:12:33,833
Karen! Deploy them
to Soriano Street.

239
00:12:33,967 --> 00:12:36,367
- Yes, sir. Get going.
- Yes, ma'am.

240
00:12:37,467 --> 00:12:39,033
[MANNY]
Is Director Delgado here?

241
00:12:39,167 --> 00:12:42,133
Tell him
General Ricardo Jacinto is here.

242
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:45,933
[SEBASTIAN] Sir! Good morning.

243
00:12:46,067 --> 00:12:50,167
Are you here to get updates
about the search for Sam?

244
00:12:50,333 --> 00:12:54,000
Well, I can assure you that we
at the NCIA are doing our job.

245
00:12:54,100 --> 00:12:56,567
Well, you should've begun
the investigation.

246
00:12:57,333 --> 00:12:58,567
Starting last night!

247
00:12:58,733 --> 00:13:01,300
Would you like to know
what I did?

248
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:05,167
- I mean, what the team did.
- Of course!

249
00:13:05,267 --> 00:13:08,200
Alright, sir. Let's go upstairs.
Follow me, sir.

250
00:13:12,433 --> 00:13:14,300
[INDISTINCT CONVERSATION]

251
00:13:16,767 --> 00:13:21,833
[INDISTINCT CONVERSATION]

252
00:13:21,967 --> 00:13:23,100
[TEKLA] She's here.

253
00:13:24,233 --> 00:13:25,667
- She might hear you.
- Oh.

254
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:29,233
I heard there was
a shootout here last night.

255
00:13:29,367 --> 00:13:30,267
What happened?

256
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:39,200
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

257
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:41,767
You had something to do
with the mess, didn't you, Gabo?

258
00:13:41,933 --> 00:13:45,033
[TEKLA] Wow, Miss Betchay!

259
00:13:45,133 --> 00:13:46,833
You just arrived, but
you're already pointing fingers!

260
00:13:46,967 --> 00:13:49,000
Gabo had nothing to do
with what happened last night!

261
00:13:49,133 --> 00:13:52,233
- You're too judgmental.
- I was just making sure!

262
00:13:52,967 --> 00:13:55,433
I've just been promoted
to manager.

263
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:57,467
I don't want to get involved
in any mess.

264
00:13:59,667 --> 00:14:01,267
Manager!

265
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:03,567
Manager!
[CHCUKLING]

266
00:14:03,667 --> 00:14:05,633
- Here.
- [TEKLA] Nice one.

267
00:14:06,467 --> 00:14:07,467
For you.

268
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:09,767
It came from Paquito
because of me.

269
00:14:09,900 --> 00:14:12,867
You get to eat good food now.
[CHUCKLING]

270
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,133
I'm going to sleep now, okay?

271
00:14:14,267 --> 00:14:15,800
My god,
I was so tired last night.

272
00:14:15,967 --> 00:14:20,933
But it's such a good feeling
to attain your dream.

273
00:14:21,067 --> 00:14:26,133
That you see your hard work
paying off!

274
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:29,133
So long as you do
the right thing.

275
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:31,967
And you're not just
full of words.

276
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:36,167
Move!

277
00:14:37,033 --> 00:14:42,267
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

278
00:14:42,367 --> 00:14:44,933
[SAM]<i> Oh no.
</i> They're going to catch me.

279
00:14:46,967 --> 00:14:47,900
Ahh!

280
00:14:48,667 --> 00:14:49,900
Is there food here?

281
00:14:50,033 --> 00:14:53,133
[SAM]<i> But before they catch me,
</i> I have to strike first.

282
00:14:53,267 --> 00:14:54,267
[CURTAIN RATTLES]

283
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:57,967
Should I eat? Coffee.

284
00:14:59,967 --> 00:15:06,933
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

285
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:13,700
[BAG THUDS]

286
00:15:14,333 --> 00:15:15,367
[GROANS]

287
00:15:16,567 --> 00:15:23,500
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

288
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:28,100
Sir, as you can see,
we started the search

289
00:15:28,233 --> 00:15:30,600
within a 2-kilometer radius
from Soriano Street,

290
00:15:30,733 --> 00:15:32,933
where we found Sam's car.

291
00:15:33,067 --> 00:15:37,700
There is a good chance that
if Sam ran from Soriano Street,

292
00:15:37,867 --> 00:15:41,033
she could've ended up
in the surrounding communities.

293
00:15:41,700 --> 00:15:45,733
So, sir, by the way,
have you received any calls?

294
00:15:45,867 --> 00:15:47,733
Like, random demands,

295
00:15:47,867 --> 00:15:50,400
anonymous calls,
or cryptic messages?

296
00:15:50,567 --> 00:15:52,967
- Nothing.
- Then...

297
00:15:53,100 --> 00:15:55,167
As of now, we have no indication

298
00:15:55,267 --> 00:15:56,733
that this is
a kidnap-for-ransom case.

299
00:15:56,900 --> 00:15:59,533
- But I have a theory.
- I don't need your damn theory!

300
00:15:59,667 --> 00:16:01,067
I need results!

301
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:02,733
It's a confirmed ambush!

302
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:05,633
Why has no one been
arrested or interrogated?

303
00:16:05,767 --> 00:16:07,733
Because we do not have
sufficient evidence

304
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:09,567
to determine
who ordered this attack, sir.

305
00:16:09,767 --> 00:16:10,733
[SLAMS HAND ON TABLE]

306
00:16:11,467 --> 00:16:14,233
We know the Zafra family
is behind this!

307
00:16:14,367 --> 00:16:15,767
They are our suspects,

308
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:18,433
but suspicion isn't enough
for us to arrest them.

309
00:16:19,200 --> 00:16:22,933
So why isn't anybody
interrogating Victor Zafra?!

310
00:16:23,067 --> 00:16:24,533
[DELGADO] I've talked to him.

311
00:16:24,633 --> 00:16:25,667
Sir.

312
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:28,100
He denied everything.

313
00:16:28,767 --> 00:16:30,333
Of course, he will!

314
00:16:30,467 --> 00:16:32,667
What criminal will admit
to his crime?!

315
00:16:32,800 --> 00:16:34,767
[DELGADO] Ricardo, calm down.

316
00:16:34,933 --> 00:16:37,600
Let's talk in my office.
Please follow me.

317
00:16:39,900 --> 00:16:43,667
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

318
00:16:43,833 --> 00:16:45,033
We have a big problem.

319
00:16:45,667 --> 00:16:49,300
If Mama Betchay finds out
that woman is staying here,

320
00:16:49,433 --> 00:16:52,733
I'm sure Paquito will know
about it.

321
00:16:52,833 --> 00:16:54,233
Everyone in our community
will know!

322
00:16:54,333 --> 00:16:56,233
How will we hide her Gabo?

323
00:16:56,333 --> 00:16:59,433
Your rooms are practically
next to each other!

324
00:16:59,567 --> 00:17:01,633
We'll find a way.

325
00:17:01,767 --> 00:17:04,967
But, Gabo, we can't hide this
from Betchay for long.

326
00:17:05,100 --> 00:17:08,533
[MAMENG] That's right!
Betchay's only sleeping now

327
00:17:08,667 --> 00:17:10,467
because she's exhausted.

328
00:17:10,633 --> 00:17:13,867
Don't worry.
Betchay is a heavy sleeper.

329
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,700
Even if Ginintuang Lupa
ends up in flames,

330
00:17:16,867 --> 00:17:18,833
I'm sure she won't wake up!

331
00:17:18,967 --> 00:17:21,333
But still!
They're both gonna wake up!

332
00:17:21,500 --> 00:17:24,000
What if they wake up
at the same time?

333
00:17:24,167 --> 00:17:26,167
[DANTE] That will be
our new problem.

334
00:17:26,333 --> 00:17:28,100
I mean, look at our problem
with Rudy.

335
00:17:28,200 --> 00:17:30,933
We still don't know
who shot him.

336
00:17:31,033 --> 00:17:33,833
And there's the issue
with the Jacintos

337
00:17:33,967 --> 00:17:35,967
who want Ginintuang Lupa.

338
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:38,000
We can resolve all those.

339
00:17:38,167 --> 00:17:40,767
But can you not mention
those Jacintos?!

340
00:17:40,867 --> 00:17:41,967
No matter what happens,

341
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:44,333
they'll never take
Ginintuang Lupa from us!

342
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:46,433
[MAMENG] Rudy, Rudy.
This isn't good for you.

343
00:17:46,533 --> 00:17:48,833
Come, let's go inside
and calm down.

344
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,867
This won't be good
for your wounds, come on.

345
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:52,500
You haven't even healed yet.

346
00:17:52,633 --> 00:17:53,500
Oh.

347
00:17:53,633 --> 00:17:56,033
[TEKLA] How did that woman
even come here?

348
00:17:57,067 --> 00:18:01,667
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

349
00:18:02,067 --> 00:18:03,100
- That's from last night!
- What's this?

350
00:18:03,233 --> 00:18:05,000
It's already overflowing!
I told you to cut it down!

351
00:18:05,133 --> 00:18:08,000
We'll lose money like this!
Geez, you just never listen!

352
00:18:08,133 --> 00:18:10,467
What, do you even want
to work here?

353
00:18:10,633 --> 00:18:12,767
You, so slow at pouring!

354
00:18:12,867 --> 00:18:15,033
You, so slow at rinsing!
You, so slow at scrubbing!

355
00:18:15,167 --> 00:18:16,833
- Ibyang...
- Are you three even trying?

356
00:18:16,967 --> 00:18:19,700
[PAQUITO] It's so early
and you're already hot-headed!

357
00:18:19,833 --> 00:18:22,700
Because I'm surrounded by fools!

358
00:18:22,867 --> 00:18:24,800
If not liars, then tricksters!

359
00:18:24,933 --> 00:18:27,067
And worst of all, traitors!

360
00:18:28,700 --> 00:18:30,233
Yes! Just like...

361
00:18:30,367 --> 00:18:31,467
Anyway, traitors!

362
00:18:31,600 --> 00:18:32,800
- Hmph!
- [CHUCKLES]

363
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:34,567
- Hang on. Uh...
- Hurry up!

364
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:35,867
Ibyang.

365
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:39,800
Maybe this will cool you down.

366
00:18:39,933 --> 00:18:40,800
What's that?

367
00:18:40,933 --> 00:18:44,133
This is what BeerGin earned

368
00:18:44,267 --> 00:18:47,367
on Betchay's first night
as manager.

369
00:18:47,500 --> 00:18:49,233
You just had to promote her
to manager...

370
00:18:49,367 --> 00:18:51,467
without even consulting me!

371
00:18:51,567 --> 00:18:54,000
[PAQUITO]
I knew you wouldn't agree

372
00:18:54,167 --> 00:18:57,000
because you've got bad blood
with her!

373
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:58,900
Yes, exactly!

374
00:18:59,033 --> 00:19:01,033
You knew I hate that woman,

375
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:03,333
yet you still promoted her!

376
00:19:03,433 --> 00:19:04,333
[CHUCKLES] You know what?

377
00:19:04,467 --> 00:19:06,333
The woman you look down on...

378
00:19:06,433 --> 00:19:08,533
has been attracting plenty
of customers!

379
00:19:08,700 --> 00:19:10,333
Our revenue is growing!

380
00:19:10,433 --> 00:19:11,367
[DJANGO] Pa...

381
00:19:11,533 --> 00:19:13,367
Maybe Ibyang is just afraid

382
00:19:13,533 --> 00:19:15,400
that Gabo's family is
getting close to us.

383
00:19:15,533 --> 00:19:17,000
Next thing we know,

384
00:19:17,100 --> 00:19:19,833
Betchay is feeding information
to Gabo and Rudy

385
00:19:19,933 --> 00:19:22,600
about our activities
and plans here.

386
00:19:22,733 --> 00:19:23,600
[PAQUITO SCOFFS]

387
00:19:23,733 --> 00:19:27,267
Django, there's no chance
she'll do that.

388
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:30,100
I know women like her.

389
00:19:30,667 --> 00:19:34,200
They'll side
with whoever pays them.

390
00:19:34,300 --> 00:19:36,400
Family means nothing to them.

391
00:19:36,567 --> 00:19:37,867
Come on, take it.

392
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:44,733
- [THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]
- [BOTTLES CLINKING]

393
00:19:45,267 --> 00:19:46,300
[CHUCKLES]

394
00:19:47,733 --> 00:19:48,767
Here.

395
00:19:49,833 --> 00:19:50,767
[DJANGO] Ibyang.

396
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:52,867
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

397
00:19:52,967 --> 00:19:53,933
[CHUCKLES]

398
00:19:54,467 --> 00:19:56,600
- There we go.
- It's overflowing again!

399
00:19:56,733 --> 00:19:58,633
Look, the bottle's full!
Cut it down!

400
00:19:58,767 --> 00:20:01,200
- I'm losing my patience!
- [MATET] Reduce it!

401
00:20:01,333 --> 00:20:03,100
- [DOOR OPENS]
- [MUSIC ENDS]

402
00:20:05,633 --> 00:20:07,467
I want to talk to Victor Zafra.

403
00:20:07,600 --> 00:20:09,900
We both know that
his family is behind

404
00:20:10,033 --> 00:20:11,433
everything that happened to Sam.

405
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:12,500
[DELGADO] I'm sorry, Ricardo,

406
00:20:12,633 --> 00:20:15,067
but I can't let you speak
with Victor.

407
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:16,167
First, he's a detainee.

408
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:17,967
Second, he has a lawyer.

409
00:20:18,100 --> 00:20:20,400
You are not part
of the investigating team,

410
00:20:20,500 --> 00:20:23,067
so you have no legal basis
to speak with him.

411
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:25,333
My daughter is missing,
Fernando.

412
00:20:25,467 --> 00:20:27,567
Have you forgotten?
I'm also a decorated officer.

413
00:20:27,700 --> 00:20:29,567
[DELGADO] We have to follow
the protocol.

414
00:20:29,700 --> 00:20:32,400
If you speak with him
outside of the procedure,

415
00:20:32,500 --> 00:20:34,633
this will be used by his lawyer

416
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:37,833
to question everything
the agency does!

417
00:20:37,967 --> 00:20:39,433
So what do you want me to do?!

418
00:20:39,567 --> 00:20:40,433
Wait?!

419
00:20:40,567 --> 00:20:41,800
I want you...

420
00:20:41,967 --> 00:20:43,167
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

421
00:20:43,300 --> 00:20:45,100
to let us do our job!

422
00:20:45,867 --> 00:20:47,100
That's easy for you to say

423
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:48,833
because it's not your child
who's gone missing.

424
00:20:50,733 --> 00:20:51,767
[DOOR OPENS]

425
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:55,667
Try to calm down for now.
Drink some water.

426
00:20:56,633 --> 00:20:58,267
Here you go. Drink it.

427
00:20:58,400 --> 00:20:59,367
Thank you.

428
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:00,933
- [MAMENG] My goodness.
- [GULPING]

429
00:21:01,033 --> 00:21:02,000
[GLASS THUDS]

430
00:21:03,200 --> 00:21:04,533
- Rudy...
- [CHAIR SCRAPES]

431
00:21:05,367 --> 00:21:07,367
Let's talk.

432
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:09,800
Is Gabo doing the right thing?

433
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:11,733
Mameng, what can we do?

434
00:21:11,867 --> 00:21:13,633
She needs our help.

435
00:21:13,733 --> 00:21:15,133
Gabo is right.

436
00:21:16,067 --> 00:21:17,200
You have a point.

437
00:21:17,333 --> 00:21:18,967
[RUDY] You know Gabo.

438
00:21:19,733 --> 00:21:21,633
He has a heart
for those in need.

439
00:21:21,767 --> 00:21:22,667
You know that.

440
00:21:22,833 --> 00:21:25,133
Listen, Betchay can't find out
about this.

441
00:21:25,267 --> 00:21:29,233
Because the moment that woman
discovers we're hiding someone

442
00:21:29,367 --> 00:21:31,300
that the cops are looking for...

443
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:33,300
Oh, she's going to go berserk.

444
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:37,333
She'll have another mouth
to feed under this roof.

445
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:40,467
You know how she counts
every single can of sardines,

446
00:21:40,567 --> 00:21:41,967
how many pieces of bread
there are.

447
00:21:42,100 --> 00:21:43,167
Even the grains of rice,

448
00:21:43,267 --> 00:21:45,033
that woman knows them all!

449
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:47,533
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

450
00:21:47,700 --> 00:21:50,333
General Jacinto didn't like
what we did.

451
00:21:52,033 --> 00:21:53,733
[KAREN] Based on Sam's stories,

452
00:21:53,867 --> 00:21:56,667
he has high expectations
of everyone.

453
00:21:56,767 --> 00:21:59,067
Even Sir Seb couldn't impress
the General.

454
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:00,933
[SEQIOA] Actually,
it makes me wonder

455
00:22:01,067 --> 00:22:05,333
what kind of NLEA Chief he was
back in his younger days.

456
00:22:05,467 --> 00:22:06,400
What do you think?

457
00:22:06,533 --> 00:22:07,833
Ferocious.

458
00:22:07,933 --> 00:22:08,933
Terrifying.

459
00:22:09,067 --> 00:22:10,167
Ruthless.

460
00:22:11,133 --> 00:22:13,400
Well, any father
in his situation

461
00:22:13,533 --> 00:22:17,000
would bare his fangs
for his child.

462
00:22:17,167 --> 00:22:19,700
Oh, sir, we almost
forgot about your theory.

463
00:22:19,800 --> 00:22:20,867
Please share it with the team!

464
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:21,867
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

465
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:23,533
Would you like
to hear my theory?

466
00:22:23,633 --> 00:22:24,600
- Yes, sir!
- [SCOFFS]

467
00:22:24,733 --> 00:22:25,600
Alright, listen up.

468
00:22:25,733 --> 00:22:27,867
Sam and I have
this special connection.

469
00:22:27,967 --> 00:22:29,633
We're thick as thieves. Right?

470
00:22:30,233 --> 00:22:31,600
So I know how her mind works.

471
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:33,367
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

472
00:22:33,467 --> 00:22:34,533
Then explain it to us.

473
00:22:35,467 --> 00:22:38,267
Sam has been suspended
from the NCIA, remember?

474
00:22:38,433 --> 00:22:40,267
She won't show herself to us

475
00:22:40,433 --> 00:22:43,967
because she's continuing
her investigation.

476
00:22:44,133 --> 00:22:47,233
She wants us to think
she's missing,

477
00:22:47,333 --> 00:22:49,100
or even dead,

478
00:22:49,300 --> 00:22:52,767
so she can freely pursue the
investigation she's working on.

479
00:22:52,867 --> 00:22:54,800
Sir, you're a genius!

480
00:22:54,967 --> 00:22:57,400
- Such a believable idea!
- It's possible, right?

481
00:22:57,500 --> 00:22:58,467
We're close.

482
00:22:58,600 --> 00:22:59,767
Come on, Uncle.

483
00:22:59,867 --> 00:23:01,400
You know Papa
hasn't fully recovered yet.

484
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:02,467
Why tell him that?

485
00:23:02,600 --> 00:23:04,467
I know. I just blurted it out.

486
00:23:04,600 --> 00:23:06,300
Gabo, are you serious?

487
00:23:06,467 --> 00:23:08,633
You're going to let that woman
stay in your house?

488
00:23:09,333 --> 00:23:11,133
Where will she sleep?

489
00:23:11,267 --> 00:23:12,233
Right next to you?

490
00:23:12,767 --> 00:23:13,733
Tekla.

491
00:23:13,833 --> 00:23:15,300
So what if she does?

492
00:23:15,867 --> 00:23:17,733
I don't have any bad intentions
toward her.

493
00:23:17,833 --> 00:23:19,467
Sure, you don't.

494
00:23:19,633 --> 00:23:20,633
But what about her?

495
00:23:20,767 --> 00:23:21,800
[SILLY MUSIC PLAYING]

496
00:23:21,967 --> 00:23:24,533
Gabo, I'm only worried for you.

497
00:23:27,867 --> 00:23:28,933
It's final.

498
00:23:29,833 --> 00:23:33,333
She'll stay here as long
as her life is in danger.

499
00:23:35,867 --> 00:23:40,700
[SILLY MUSIC CONTINUES]

500
00:23:40,867 --> 00:23:41,933
- [BINOY] Gabo!
- [TEKLA] Hey!

501
00:23:42,033 --> 00:23:43,267
- Gabo...
- What is it?

502
00:23:44,133 --> 00:23:45,167
What's going on?

503
00:23:45,333 --> 00:23:46,667
Hang on, I'll join you.

504
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:48,033
[HURRIED FOOTSTEPS]

505
00:23:48,733 --> 00:23:50,333
- Let's check it out!
- I agree!

506
00:23:50,500 --> 00:23:51,867
- Gabo...
- What did you see?

507
00:23:52,033 --> 00:23:53,033
[SAM] He saw me!

508
00:23:53,700 --> 00:23:55,100
<i> I need to think fast!</i>

509
00:23:55,200 --> 00:24:00,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

510
00:24:00,533 --> 00:24:01,367
[GABO GRUNTS]

511
00:24:01,500 --> 00:24:03,067
Who are you, huh?!

512
00:24:03,233 --> 00:24:04,533
What's your name?!

513
00:24:05,333 --> 00:24:06,467
I'm sure General
will listen to me

514
00:24:06,600 --> 00:24:07,967
once he hears my theory.

515
00:24:08,067 --> 00:24:10,500
Sir, my theory about Sam...

516
00:24:10,667 --> 00:24:11,833
To hell with your theory!

517
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:14,500
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

518
00:24:14,600 --> 00:24:15,733
This is your fault!

519
00:24:15,867 --> 00:24:17,700
You failed to protect
my daughter!

520
00:24:17,867 --> 00:24:21,733
She chose the NCIA
over the NLEA.

521
00:24:21,867 --> 00:24:24,500
And now this?
This is what happens to her?

522
00:24:25,867 --> 00:24:27,067
Useless!

523
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:28,733
Your agency is useless!

524
00:24:28,900 --> 00:24:33,233
Ricardo, don't think
we've abandoned Sam.

525
00:24:33,400 --> 00:24:35,867
Finding her is the
NCIA's top priority.

526
00:24:36,033 --> 00:24:38,600
And if the Zafras
are behind this,

527
00:24:38,733 --> 00:24:41,533
we'll find the evidence
to prove it.

528
00:24:41,900 --> 00:24:43,100
I'm sorry, Fernando.

529
00:24:43,233 --> 00:24:45,000
I've lost faith in the NCIA.

530
00:24:45,100 --> 00:24:46,200
And if I were you,

531
00:24:46,367 --> 00:24:49,233
I'd transfer Victor Zafra
to maximum security

532
00:24:50,100 --> 00:24:51,933
so his family
can't break him out.

533
00:24:52,067 --> 00:24:56,000
Victor's our only link
to the Zafras.

534
00:24:56,100 --> 00:24:57,400
He stays here

535
00:24:57,567 --> 00:24:59,433
while the investigation's
ongoing.

536
00:24:59,567 --> 00:25:03,067
Delgado, you don't know
what the Zafras are planning,

537
00:25:03,267 --> 00:25:04,367
and neither do I!

538
00:25:04,467 --> 00:25:06,800
They could blow up
this entire NCIA

539
00:25:06,933 --> 00:25:08,400
just to get Victor out!

540
00:25:08,567 --> 00:25:09,933
So I'm telling you now...

541
00:25:10,100 --> 00:25:11,400
I strongly recommend

542
00:25:11,567 --> 00:25:13,567
transferring him
to maximum security

543
00:25:14,333 --> 00:25:16,067
so he can be properly guarded.

544
00:25:16,233 --> 00:25:20,267
Ricardo, I know why
you're doing this.

545
00:25:20,433 --> 00:25:22,533
You just want revenge
on the Zafras.

546
00:25:23,467 --> 00:25:24,767
No, Fernando.

547
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:29,633
I'm doing this as a father.

548
00:25:31,833 --> 00:25:33,567
It's something I haven't been
able to do for Samantha

549
00:25:33,733 --> 00:25:34,900
for a long...

550
00:25:35,300 --> 00:25:36,500
long time.

551
00:25:36,767 --> 00:25:39,400
[PHONE RINGING]

552
00:25:39,500 --> 00:25:41,233
General Jacinto, it's the judge.

553
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:49,133
Your Honor?

554
00:25:49,300 --> 00:25:54,133
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

555
00:25:54,800 --> 00:25:55,933
Thank you.

556
00:26:00,967 --> 00:26:02,633
The court's issuing an order

557
00:26:03,133 --> 00:26:07,067
demanding that the NCIA
transfer Victor Zafra

558
00:26:08,667 --> 00:26:10,333
to maximum security.

559
00:26:13,300 --> 00:26:14,300
Today.

560
00:26:14,400 --> 00:26:19,167
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

561
00:26:22,700 --> 00:26:25,767
Team, conference room. Now!

562
00:26:25,867 --> 00:26:30,133
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

563
00:26:30,667 --> 00:26:31,700
[MUSIC STOPS]

564
00:26:31,833 --> 00:26:32,933
What's your name?

565
00:26:33,033 --> 00:26:34,133
What was that?

566
00:26:34,233 --> 00:26:35,333
It's Gabo!

567
00:26:36,133 --> 00:26:37,767
[GRUNTING] Don't point that gun!

568
00:26:37,867 --> 00:26:39,767
That thing's possessed!
It might go off!

569
00:26:39,867 --> 00:26:41,500
I'm really going to shoot you!

570
00:26:41,700 --> 00:26:42,667
Who are you?

571
00:26:42,833 --> 00:26:44,200
[GABO GRUNTING]

572
00:26:44,367 --> 00:26:45,833
- Oh, no!
- Don't come any closer!

573
00:26:45,933 --> 00:26:47,367
Miss, miss!

574
00:26:47,533 --> 00:26:50,200
Don't! You might fire it!
Calm down, miss!

575
00:26:51,200 --> 00:26:53,033
[SAM]
<i> I need to keep pretending.</i>

576
00:26:53,200 --> 00:26:54,967
<i> If they find out, I'm dead.</i>

577
00:26:56,200 --> 00:26:57,367
Looks like the woman is awake.

578
00:26:57,533 --> 00:26:59,067
She might do
something to Gabo!

579
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:00,500
- Come on, let's help him.
- No!

580
00:27:00,600 --> 00:27:01,567
What are you doing?

581
00:27:01,700 --> 00:27:03,133
She's NCIA, right?
She's got a gun!

582
00:27:03,233 --> 00:27:04,700
What if they start shooting
in there?

583
00:27:04,867 --> 00:27:06,167
Lower your gun.

584
00:27:06,267 --> 00:27:07,667
What am I doing here?!

585
00:27:07,767 --> 00:27:08,833
Why am I here?!

586
00:27:08,933 --> 00:27:11,167
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

587
00:27:11,333 --> 00:27:12,333
Hey!

588
00:27:12,433 --> 00:27:14,500
- [MAMENG GASPS]
- [BETCHAY] Who's that?

589
00:27:14,600 --> 00:27:17,133
If you're not going to sleep,
at least let the others sleep!

590
00:27:17,867 --> 00:27:19,200
Keep your voice down, please.

591
00:27:19,367 --> 00:27:20,833
[TOLITS] It's Gabo.

592
00:27:20,933 --> 00:27:22,700
He keeps bringing
all sorts of people in.

593
00:27:22,867 --> 00:27:24,267
Why'd he let her stay here?

594
00:27:24,400 --> 00:27:25,867
They're only going to get
themselves in trouble.

595
00:27:26,033 --> 00:27:27,367
We'll get dragged
into this, too.

596
00:27:27,467 --> 00:27:29,433
Oh, gosh! If anything
happens to Gabo,

597
00:27:29,567 --> 00:27:31,167
that woman is going
to answer to me.

598
00:27:31,267 --> 00:27:33,167
She won't leave
Ginintuang Lupa alive!

599
00:27:33,267 --> 00:27:35,867
Tekla, nothing's going
to happen to Gabo.

600
00:27:36,033 --> 00:27:38,233
And Gabo can handle
that woman.

601
00:27:38,400 --> 00:27:39,367
He's right.

602
00:27:39,467 --> 00:27:41,400
Besides, Sir Rudy and
Miss Mameng are there.

603
00:27:41,567 --> 00:27:43,100
Maybe they're just talking.

604
00:27:43,233 --> 00:27:44,567
[HUFFS] I hate this!

605
00:27:44,733 --> 00:27:46,433
- [GABO EXHALING]
- [RUDY] Easy, easy!

606
00:27:46,567 --> 00:27:48,833
Miss... [BREATHING HEAVILY]

607
00:27:48,967 --> 00:27:50,567
Lower your gun.

608
00:27:50,733 --> 00:27:52,400
[GASPING] It might go off!

609
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:55,433
We'll explain everything.

610
00:27:56,400 --> 00:27:57,800
[GABO GRUNTING]

611
00:27:57,933 --> 00:28:02,400
Miss, miss, we'll explain
everything calmly.

612
00:28:02,500 --> 00:28:03,867
Let's put the gun down

613
00:28:03,967 --> 00:28:06,233
so he can explain
what happened.

614
00:28:06,767 --> 00:28:10,700
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

615
00:28:10,800 --> 00:28:12,733
[SAM] I need to think fast.

616
00:28:13,567 --> 00:28:15,400
<i> I can't leave this house.</i>

617
00:28:16,133 --> 00:28:17,733
<i> Right now...</i>

618
00:28:18,833 --> 00:28:20,567
this is the only place I'm safe.

619
00:28:21,400 --> 00:28:25,900
<i>I need to pretend for now
so they won't make me leave.</i>

620
00:28:27,300 --> 00:28:29,233
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

621
00:28:29,333 --> 00:28:30,567
Who am I?!

622
00:28:32,100 --> 00:28:33,567
Rudy, I think...

623
00:28:34,133 --> 00:28:37,667
I think she hit her head
when she fell.

624
00:28:38,200 --> 00:28:39,333
Yeah.

625
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:42,567
We'll talk about that later.
Put the gun down first!

626
00:28:42,667 --> 00:28:44,600
[GABO]
<i> She's not in her right mind!</i>

627
00:28:44,700 --> 00:28:46,600
What did he do to me?
Why am I here?

628
00:28:46,767 --> 00:28:49,167
<i>I need to pretend
so she won't leave this place.</i>

629
00:28:49,300 --> 00:28:52,400
<i>Otherwise,
her life will be in danger.</i>

630
00:28:53,467 --> 00:28:55,500
- [GABO GRUNTING]
- Who are you?!

631
00:28:56,667 --> 00:28:58,700
[GRUNTING]

632
00:28:59,367 --> 00:29:00,467
Honey!

633
00:29:00,567 --> 00:29:01,700
[GROANS]

634
00:29:01,833 --> 00:29:05,300
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

635
00:29:05,900 --> 00:29:07,633
You're Gloria!

636
00:29:08,200 --> 00:29:09,933
I'm your husband, Gabo!

637
00:29:10,033 --> 00:29:16,200
[MUSIC BECOMES QUIRKY]

638
00:29:16,667 --> 00:29:18,033
<i> Once Victor's transferred,</i>

639
00:29:18,167 --> 00:29:19,600
it'll be harder to get him out.

640
00:29:19,700 --> 00:29:22,333
<i>They haven't even charged me
with anything!</i>

641
00:29:22,500 --> 00:29:23,867
<i> You're useless!</i>

642
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:25,633
<i> I don't trust the NCIA.</i>

643
00:29:25,733 --> 00:29:27,333
<i>I want you to be part
of the transfer.</i>

644
00:29:27,500 --> 00:29:30,167
<i>He's questioning
the NCIA's capabilities.</i>

645
00:29:30,367 --> 00:29:31,700
<i> We have to prove to him</i>

646
00:29:31,867 --> 00:29:34,633
that we can find solid evidence
<i> against the Zafras.</i>

647
00:29:34,733 --> 00:29:37,167
<i>You need to move fast.
There'll be plenty of escorts.</i>

648
00:29:37,267 --> 00:29:39,500
<i>Pia, signal Victor
when it's time.</i>

649
00:29:39,600 --> 00:29:40,900
<i>- Get the men ready.
- Yes, sir.</i>

650
00:29:41,033 --> 00:29:42,300
<i> This is our best chance.</i>

651
00:29:42,400 --> 00:29:44,000
I'll bring your son home later.

652
00:29:44,100 --> 00:29:45,967
<i>We've got a problem.
She can't remember anything.</i>

653
00:29:46,067 --> 00:29:47,300
<i> We need to help her.</i>

654
00:29:47,400 --> 00:29:49,233
<i> You think you can fool me?</i>

655
00:29:49,367 --> 00:29:51,833
<i>I'll find out what your
connection to Zafra is.</i>

656
00:29:51,933 --> 00:29:53,367
<i>Because once that woman
finds out</i>

657
00:29:53,533 --> 00:29:55,133
<i>none of what we're
telling her is true,</i>

658
00:29:55,233 --> 00:29:56,167
<i> she'll leave for sure.</i>

659
00:29:56,333 --> 00:29:57,967
Her enemies are waiting outside

660
00:29:58,067 --> 00:29:59,133
<i> and they'll kill her!</i>

661
00:29:59,233 --> 00:30:01,067
<i>If I'm your wife,
do we have kids?</i>

662
00:30:01,200 --> 00:30:05,000
<i>We've tried to have kids
many times,</i>

663
00:30:05,133 --> 00:30:07,200
<i>but God hasn't blessed us
with any yet.</i>

664
00:30:07,367 --> 00:30:09,600
<i>Don't worry.
Tonight, we'll make a baby.</i>
